  "answer_text": "Under Brazilian law, specifically Law No. 12,506/2011 (Article 1), the statutory notice period for an employee with exactly one year of continuous service is 30 days. The law establishes a base of 30 days for employees with up to one year of service and adds 3 days for each additional year of service, capped at a total of 90 days. Since the employee has completed exactly one full year but not yet entered their second year of service, no additional days are accrued beyond the initial 30-day base.",
  "answer_type": "duration",
  "structured_fields": [
